# ---- the PR-dependency gate and the tip-red arm (BH-629, optional — ON is the default) ----
# Every automatic merge path asks the gate whether the PR body declares a
# dependency — a `Depends on #N (PR #M)` line — and holds the merge while that
# dependency is still open. #615 merged over its own open #609 and left main red
# for 7.5 hours; that is the incident the gate exists for.
# 0 = the lanes merge as they did before the gate. A rollback switch, not a
# tuning knob; `flags/pr-dep-gate-off` is the same switch as a file.
# The parser landed with BH-629.1; the lane calls land with BH-629.2. Until then
# the knob is documented and read by pdg_enabled, and it changes nothing.
#PR_DEP_GATE=0
# The tip-red arm of bin/main-red-detector.sh: declare main red on the FIRST red
# run on its tip, once that run is old enough not to be a re-run in flight.
# 0 = only the MAIN_RED_STREAK arm fires, which needs a second red run that can
# only arrive from the very merge the red is preventing. Lands with BH-629.4.
#MAIN_RED_TIP_RED=0
# How many minutes the red run on main's tip must have stood before that arm
# fires. Lands with BH-629.4.
#MAIN_RED_TIP_MIN_AGE_MIN=15
# The two ways a PR merges THROUGH a main-red freeze. Both were read only by
# bin/merge-conductor.sh until BH-945; they are fleet-wide now, read by
# bin/lib/main-red-gate.sh on behalf of every merge lane (the conductor, the hub
# merge sweep, the box merge queue, the reviewer, the tier-2 sweep, the tier-1
# gate inside a build and the union merge train). Changing either changes what
# lands while main is broken, so change them on the hub and the boxes together.
# The label is matched by EXACT name, so `fix-main-red-later` is not it.
#MC_MAIN_RED_LABEL=fix-main-red
# Space-separated `case` globs. A PR is exempt only if EVERY file in its diff
# matches one of them; a diff that cannot be read is never exempt.
#MC_MAIN_RED_TEST_PATHS=tests/* worker/*/test/*

